The two folders dsh-subagent-claude-code and dsh-subagent-codex hold lib/index.js and package.json
of the npm packages @deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-claude-code and @deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-codex,
version 0.1.5-rc.2 (repository https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, folders
packages/subagent/subagent-claude-code and packages/subagent/subagent-codex), copied from the published
packages byte for byte but for one character: the em-dash in each file's "no working directory"
error is a hyphen here, since this repository keeps that character out of every file. They are the connector files scripts/patch-agent-live.mjs is written
against, kept here so its tests patch exactly what the harness installs (test/patch-agent-live.test.js).

The folder stubs holds small stand-ins, written for these tests, for the packages those files
import: @deepseek-ai/schemastery, dsh-timeout, dsh-subagent, dsh-brand, dsh-subprocess and
dsh-sdk-protocol, @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk and @openai/codex. They are not copies of those
packages.

